WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.643
Welcome to EstateAegis.

2
00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:07.256
In the next few minutes,

3
00:00:07.266 --> 00:00:10.631
we'll walk through a typical week for a home watch company,

4
00:00:10.641 --> 00:00:15.295
from the first visit of the day, to the storm that tests everyone's planning.

5
00:00:17.445 --> 00:00:20.287
Everything you'll see is demonstration data,

6
00:00:20.297 --> 00:00:23.724
in a sample company called Harborline Home Watch.

7
00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:27.775
Your team signs in at estateaegis.com.

8
00:00:27.785 --> 00:00:32.992
Owners, staff, families, and vendors each get a view made for them.

9
00:00:37.242 --> 00:00:40.196
After signing in, you land on the Overview.

10
00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:46.393
The first line tells you what needs you today: failed items, reports to sign,

11
00:00:46.403 --> 00:00:49.615
overdue visits, and new requests from clients.

12
00:00:50.865 --> 00:00:52.738
Needs your attention lists each one,

13
00:00:52.748 --> 00:00:55.300
with a button that takes you straight to it.

14
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.657
Today's visits sit on the right.

15
00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:03.223
Plan today's route picks the homes that are due, lets you add others,

16
00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:05.865
and opens directions in Google Maps.

17
00:01:07.115 --> 00:01:11.823
The menu on the left is grouped the way you work: daily work, residences,

18
00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:12.986
team, and company.

19
00:01:12.996 --> 00:01:16.154
Each group folds away when you don't need it.

20
00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:23.850
Residences shows every home you look after, with its family and photo.

21
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.052
Open one, and the Summary pulls together what needs attention,

22
00:01:29.062 --> 00:01:33.529
upcoming visits, open work, the next arrival, and the latest note.

23
00:01:34.779 --> 00:01:39.740
Home records keeps equipment, maintenance plans, documents, the house manual,

24
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.389
and access codes with the right home.

25
00:01:43.639 --> 00:01:46.731
And People shows the family, the residence manager,

26
00:01:46.741 --> 00:01:49.180
and who on your team looks after it.

27
00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.555
Smart locks are kept in Home records too.

28
00:01:54.565 --> 00:01:58.892
Add each lock at the residence, from your connected lock account,

29
00:01:58.902 --> 00:02:00.353
or in manual mode.

30
00:02:02.403 --> 00:02:07.201
Every visit or job with an assignee gets its own temporary door code,

31
00:02:07.211 --> 00:02:10.179
good only for that visit's time window.

32
00:02:12.029 --> 00:02:16.373
Your team member sees the code on their phone only during the window.

33
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:18.265
Families never see door codes,

34
00:02:18.275 --> 00:02:21.554
and every view is recorded in the audit history.

35
00:02:25.004 --> 00:02:30.246
Many insurance policies require regular checks while a home is unoccupied.

36
00:02:30.256 --> 00:02:35.073
In Home records, add the policy, how often the home must be visited,

37
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:37.817
and the longest it may stay vacant.

38
00:02:39.867 --> 00:02:45.086
The Insurance compliance page shows every residence as OK, Due soon, At risk,

39
00:02:45.096 --> 00:02:48.809
or Breached, with the reason and the next deadline.

40
00:02:50.859 --> 00:02:54.093
And a visit history certificate is ready to download,

41
00:02:54.103 --> 00:02:56.067
or to share with the broker.

42
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:01.249
Every visit follows a checklist.

43
00:03:01.259 --> 00:03:04.666
Start from a ready-made template, or build your own.

44
00:03:05.916 --> 00:03:09.698
Each item is answered Pass, Monitor, Fail, or N/A.

45
00:03:10.948 --> 00:03:14.132
You can require photos, mark items as required,

46
00:03:14.142 --> 00:03:18.061
and choose which failures alert the office right away.

47
00:03:21.111 --> 00:03:23.240
Now, let's head out on a visit.

48
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.157
EstateAegis works on any phone, right in the browser.

49
00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:30.781
Checking in records the GPS location,

50
00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:34.908
so every report shows the visit really happened at the home.

51
00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:38.712
Then work through the checklist.

52
00:03:38.722 --> 00:03:41.366
Tap Fail, add a note, and take a photo.

53
00:03:43.516 --> 00:03:44.162
No signal?

54
00:03:44.172 --> 00:03:44.884
Keep going.

55
00:03:44.894 --> 00:03:47.639
Answers and photos are saved on the phone,

56
00:03:47.649 --> 00:03:51.245
and they sync on their own once you're back online.

57
00:03:58.495 --> 00:04:03.249
Photo spots capture the same view, from the same angle, on every visit.

58
00:04:03.259 --> 00:04:08.608
Each spot has a baseline photo, like the water heater or the pool equipment.

59
00:04:10.658 --> 00:04:14.877
On the visit, the camera shows the baseline as a see-through overlay,

60
00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.731
so the new photo lines up.

61
00:04:19.381 --> 00:04:24.793
Reports then place each photo beside its baseline, so changes are easy to see.

62
00:04:28.043 --> 00:04:30.219
Once an administrator turns it on,

63
00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:34.849
Draft summary with AI writes a first draft of the visit summary from the

64
00:04:34.859 --> 00:04:36.909
checklist answers and notes.

65
00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:42.616
Use this draft, try again, or discard it.

66
00:04:42.626 --> 00:04:47.442
Nothing written by AI reaches a family until someone on your team has

67
00:04:47.452 --> 00:04:50.359
reviewed it and confirmed the summary.

68
00:04:53.809 --> 00:04:58.594
When a visit comes in with a failed item, the office is alerted right away,

69
00:04:58.604 --> 00:05:00.388
in the app and by email.

70
00:05:01.638 --> 00:05:05.520
Review the report, then publish it to the family with one click.

71
00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:11.699
The PDF carries your company's name and logo, with photos, notes,

72
00:05:11.709 --> 00:05:13.845
and the visit verification.

73
00:05:16.495 --> 00:05:18.940
Any finding can become a work order.

74
00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:23.578
The board groups jobs by due date, with quick filters, like overdue,

75
00:05:23.588 --> 00:05:25.270
or waiting on client.

76
00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.940
Assign a job to someone on your team, or to a vendor.

77
00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:34.796
When a repair needs the family's go-ahead, it waits for their approval.

78
00:05:36.546 --> 00:05:40.864
If they haven't answered yet, Remind client sends a friendly nudge.

79
00:05:40.874 --> 00:05:44.418
And Export CSV gives you the list for your records.

80
00:05:47.068 --> 00:05:52.364
Staff schedules shows the week for your whole team: shifts, visits, and jobs,

81
00:05:52.374 --> 00:05:53.796
person by person.

82
00:05:55.046 --> 00:05:58.013
Jobs that still need someone are listed below.

83
00:05:58.023 --> 00:06:00.732
Assign all hands them out in one step.

84
00:06:01.982 --> 00:06:04.046
And when severe weather is coming,

85
00:06:04.056 --> 00:06:07.173
Storm prep only narrows the week to storm work.

86
00:06:08.423 --> 00:06:13.204
The calendar lists every visit, arrival, job, and shift, day by day.

87
00:06:15.854 --> 00:06:18.970
Field inspectors get a login made just for visits.

88
00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:23.596
They see only the visits you assign them, with the address, the checklist,

89
00:06:23.606 --> 00:06:26.857
and the door codes on the day, and nothing else.

90
00:06:28.907 --> 00:06:31.314
Assign a visit in a couple of clicks.

91
00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:34.450
Every plan includes free field inspector logins,

92
00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:37.062
and they never take up a staff seat.

93
00:06:40.512 --> 00:06:44.147
Severe-weather alerts watch every residence, nationwide,

94
00:06:44.157 --> 00:06:48.442
using National Weather Service alerts and forecast thresholds.

95
00:06:50.092 --> 00:06:54.900
Hard freezes, extreme heat, floods, high wind, tornadoes, wildfire,

96
00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:55.979
and hurricanes.

97
00:06:55.989 --> 00:06:58.568
Each alert lists the homes affected,

98
00:06:58.578 --> 00:07:02.568
and the Overview shows a banner while one is active.

99
00:07:04.618 --> 00:07:06.680
Open an alert for the details.

100
00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:11.516
Start storm event creates a storm for the affected homes, in one step.

101
00:07:11.526 --> 00:07:15.437
An administrator turns alerts on in Weather settings.

102
00:07:18.887 --> 00:07:23.219
When a storm is on the way, whether it's a hurricane, a winter storm,

103
00:07:23.229 --> 00:07:25.556
or a flood, open the storm board.

104
00:07:26.806 --> 00:07:30.413
Schedule pre-storm visits for every affected home at once,

105
00:07:30.423 --> 00:07:32.170
shared across your team.

106
00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.351
The board updates on its own as homes are secured.

107
00:07:37.361 --> 00:07:42.355
After the storm, it tracks each post-storm check, and any damage found.

108
00:07:43.605 --> 00:07:48.230
And each home gets an insurance-ready storm report, with the findings,

109
00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.807
the damage notes, and dated photos.

110
00:07:53.457 --> 00:07:58.383
Families sign in on your own branded page, with your logo and your welcome.

111
00:07:59.633 --> 00:08:03.180
Their home page shows each residence, the latest reports,

112
00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:05.250
and anything waiting on them.

113
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:10.800
They can approve an estimate, send a request, or plan their next arrival,

114
00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:13.363
so the home is ready when they walk in.

115
00:08:15.113 --> 00:08:19.435
Vendors get a simple home of their own, with their jobs, due dates,

116
00:08:19.445 --> 00:08:22.734
and one tap to start work or submit completion.

117
00:08:25.384 --> 00:08:29.872
When a family adds their flight to an arrival, EstateAegis tracks it.

118
00:08:29.882 --> 00:08:33.783
Each step of the arrival plan is timed from the landing.

119
00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:40.536
If the flight is delayed, the times move with it, and your team is alerted.

120
00:08:40.546 --> 00:08:45.007
When the plan is done, the family sees that the residence is ready.

121
00:08:48.457 --> 00:08:52.437
In Company settings, add your logo, your client portal welcome,

122
00:08:52.447 --> 00:08:54.851
and your visit verification rules.

123
00:08:56.101 --> 00:08:57.283
And in My profile,

124
00:08:57.293 --> 00:09:01.779
anyone can turn on two-factor sign-in with an authenticator app.

125
00:09:05.829 --> 00:09:07.945
Switching from another system?

126
00:09:07.955 --> 00:09:13.331
Import data, under Company, brings in your clients and residences, contacts,

127
00:09:13.341 --> 00:09:15.599
vendors, staff, and past visits.

128
00:09:15.609 --> 00:09:20.040
New companies also find it on the Overview setup checklist.

129
00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:27.638
Upload a CSV or Excel export from your old software, or start from a template.

130
00:09:27.648 --> 00:09:32.388
Most columns match automatically, and you can change any match.

131
00:09:34.438 --> 00:09:38.329
The preview marks each row as new, update, or duplicate,

132
00:09:38.339 --> 00:09:40.280
with plain-English warnings.

133
00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.909
Nothing is saved until you import.

134
00:09:44.959 --> 00:09:47.499
Then a summary shows what was added.

135
00:09:47.509 --> 00:09:50.899
Undo removes the whole import within seven days.

136
00:09:50.909 --> 00:09:55.196
Imported staff stay inactive until you click Send invite.

137
00:09:58.446 --> 00:09:59.740
And that's the tour.

138
00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:04.956
EstateAegis: your residences, your team, and your clients, all in one place.

139
00:10:06.806 --> 00:10:10.618
Start your free seven-day demo at estateaegis.com.

140
00:10:10.628 --> 00:10:12.713
No credit card required.

141
00:10:14.463 --> 00:10:18.592
And when you're ready, paid plans begin with a thirty-day free trial.

142
00:10:19.842 --> 00:10:25.536
Plans include four, ten, or twenty admin and staff users, plus eight, twenty,

143
00:10:25.546 --> 00:10:28.278
or forty free field inspector logins.

144
00:10:28.288 --> 00:10:32.464
Client and vendor logins are unlimited on every plan.

